hey everyone this is sarah with  registered nurse RN comm and today i  wanted to make a quick video and show  you how to properly remove your gloves  as a nurse you're going to come into  contact with many many different germs  some germs are worse than others like  for instance as a nurse i have came in  contact with c diff MRSA VRE of one  patient i had one time had c diff and  MRSA and i had to go in the room because  they had a bowel movement how to change  them so on my gloves I had seed if I had  MRSA I had stool I had many different  things so I use this technique to remove  my gloves so I don't contaminate my  scrubs and I don't think it contaminate  my hands or any other things so if you  follow this one technique that I want to  show you you're going to dramatically  decrease your chances of becoming  contaminated our goal is to get our  gloves like this in a bowl everything  inside of the gloves so I'm going to  show you real quick how to do it first  what you'll do  here's your dirty gloves you are going  to grab the end of this cup the cup grab  the cup do not touch your arm so you're  going to grab it and you're going to  pull it completely off and then with the  glove hand you're going to hold the  glove tighten your hand then with this  unclogged hand you're going to carefully  slip it underneath the club the cup and  you're going to just slide it over that  and then we'll up everything that's  dirty and nasty is inside this glove and  then you're going to throw it away and  of course do hand hygiene wash your  hands and you're good to go so there's a  really quick video on how to remove your  gloves properly if you like this video  please subscribe to my channel and feel  free to share it with your friends and  also visit our website register in our  summer Edgecombe for a lot more nursing  school tips on how to succeed as a nurse  thank you so much and have a good day
 

